# File naming conventions

## Slides (HTML)

- `Modules/Module {N} - Slides.html` — instructor version (includes speaker notes)
- `Modules/Module {N} - Slides (Shareable).html` — shareable version (notes stripped, takeaways added)

## Module content (Markdown)

- `Modules/Module {N} - Notes (Shareable).md`
- `Modules/Module {N} - Frameworks Reference Card.md`
- `Modules/Module {N} - Glossary.md`
- `Modules/Module {N} - Pre-Read.md`

## Interactive tools (HTML)

- `Modules/M{N} - {Tool Name}.html` — single-file HTML app, vanilla JS, localStorage
- Exception: `Modules/Final Project Deliverables Builder.html` (no M6 prefix — used in M6 but produces top-level README)

## Cross-cutting

- `Modules/Concepts Primer (Pre-Read).md`
- `Modules/Frameworks Reference Card.md`
- `Modules/Glossary.md`

## Root pages (HTML)

- `index.html` — landing
- `AI Product Management - Course Overview.html`
- `Curriculum Map.html`
- `Final Project Brief.html`
- `Tools Overview.html`

## Internal docs (Markdown)

- `course-architecture.md`
- `storyline.md`
- `course-status.md`
- `README.md`

## Juno project template

- `juno-project-template/README.md` — dashboard
- `juno-project-template/{NN-name}/` — one folder per module:
  - `01-prompting/`
  - `02-strategy/`
  - `03-rag-prd/`
  - `04-ai-ux/`
  - `05-agentic-workflows/`
  - `06-evals/`
- Each subfolder has its own `README.md` + the artifact files named per module

## Pitch

- `Pitch/AI Product Management - Pitch Deck.html`
- `Pitch/Gamma Prompt.md`
